cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the paper; until it appears, cite this repository."
title: "How much of 99% accuracy survives a change of machine? A three-rig audit of bearing-fault benchmarks"
abstract: >-
  Code and result files for a three-rig audit of rolling-element bearing fault
  benchmarks. Within a dataset the benchmark is saturated; across machines
  balanced accuracy falls to between 0.039 and 0.612, and the ordering follows
  the descriptor distance between the two rigs (Spearman rho = -0.956) rather
  than the architecture.
authors:
  - family-names: "Liu"
    given-names: "Jiarui"
repository-code: "https://github.com/liu-4564/bearing-transfer-audit"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - condition monitoring
  - rolling-element bearing
  - domain shift
  - benchmark evaluation
  - reproducibility
